{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-57191",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{6}$ is $\\frac{6}{1}.$ So we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷\\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{6}{1}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\times \\frac{6}{1}=\\frac{1\\times 6}{3\\times 1}=\\frac{6}{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n6÷3=2\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
